# PPT slide style (Title + One Animation only)

Sessions are published on **YouTube (1080p)**. Every slide must be **instantly readable and focused**. Confusion is the enemy — one idea, one animation, one slide.

## Strict slide structure (non-negotiable)

1. Each slide must contain **exactly**:
   - one `## ...` heading title, and
   - one animated/interactive component (the single visual for that slide).
2. **Never** place two or more animated or interactive components under the same `##` heading.
3. **Never** add paragraph text, bullet lists, or additional UI blocks between the title and the component.
4. If a topic needs two visuals → **split into two slides** with two separate `##` headings.
5. Titles must be concise and visual-first (describe what the animation shows, not a wall of text).

## One-animation-per-component rule (for component authors)

When building a session component:

- A component may have **internal steps** (e.g. a step sequencer that plays one phase at a time), but it must present **one coherent animated idea** — not two unrelated animations stacked vertically.
- If you find yourself rendering two independent animated sections inside one component, **extract the second into its own component and its own slide**.
- Avoid side-by-side panels each running their own independent animation simultaneously; this overwhelms viewers on video.

## Diagram clarity (must-follow)

Session diagrams and interactives must be readable on video and in fullscreen presenter mode:

- **Fonts:** All interactives must follow `.cursor/rules/session-video-legibility.mdc` (body `text-lg md:text-xl`+, headings `text-xl md:text-2xl`+, **never** `text-xs`/`text-sm` for teaching copy). SVG labels: 16px+ equivalent; prefer `ui-sans-serif` / system stacks; strong contrast on both light and dark backgrounds.
- **Diagram:** Generous padding inside the canvas, clear hierarchy (one main idea per slide), labels that read without squinting at 1080p.
- **Animation:** Motions easy to follow — predictable timing, not overcrowded. One thing animates at a time where possible. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` where the component supports it.
- **Spacing:** Clear vertical space between the `##` title and the animation component — no cramming.

Layout spacing is enforced in `SessionSection` (presenter) and MDX `h2` styles (`app/sessions/[slug]/page.tsx`). New slide-style content must avoid stacking extra elements between title and animation.

When updating existing sessions, preserve this format for any newly added or edited slide content.
